{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:AppendixSurreals.OsReflectionPositivityFromReeb","@type":"LeanModule","name":"AppendixSurreals.OsReflectionPositivityFromReeb","imports":["lean:module:Init"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.OSReflectionPositivity.holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.OSReflectionPositivity.holds","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/os-reflection-positivity-from-reeb.lean#L56-L56","doc":"The categorical reflection-positivity statement. The concrete\ncontent is: for every state φ ∈ A in the positive-time Reeb\nhalf, the antipode-twisted Frobenius pairing\n⟨θ(φ), φ⟩_F is non-negative in End_C(𝟙). The class instance\nis the §3b-cond conjectural witness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.OSReflectionPositivity.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.OSReflectionPositivity.mk","kind":"ctor","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/os-reflection-positivity-from-reeb.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.OSReflectionPositivity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.OSReflectionPositivity","kind":"class","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/os-reflection-positivity-from-reeb.lean#L23-L56","doc":"**CONJECTURE.** The Frobenius pairing is positive-definite under\nthe antipodal ℤ/2 ⊂ U(1)_ξ subgroup of the Reeb U(1) — i.e. the\npairing ⟨θ(φ), φ⟩_F is non-negative for every state φ supported\non the positive-time Reeb half.\n\nThe proposition is a **parameter**: the Frobenius pairing, the Reeb\n`U(1)` and the antipode `θ` are not formalised in this file's import\ncone, so the statement cannot yet be written *about* them.\nParameterising is what lets the carrier hold the conjecture honestly\nwithout fabricating it.\n\n**Fixed 2026-09-12 (`prop-universe-field`).** The field was typed bare\n`: Prop` — the *universe* of propositions, not a proposition — so an\ninstance supplied a proposition rather than a proof of one, and\n`instance := ⟨True⟩` discharged the class. A carrier in that state\ncannot serve as a §3b conjectural witness either: it asserts nothing\n*even as a conjecture*, so a `[OSReflectionPositivity]`-conditional\ndownstream theorem was conditional on nothing. Proved for the shape in\n`QOU.ProofHygiene.SelfAssumingContexts.propUniverse_inhabited`;\ndemonstrated for named carriers in\n`docs/audits/2026-08-23-free-prop-field-triviality-probe.lean`.\n\nThe conjecture itself is untouched and still open — no instance is\nsupplied, and being contentless *for its own conjecture* is the correct\nsemantics for a conjecture carrier (§3b). What changed is that assuming\nit now costs a proof of the parameter instead of costing nothing. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:os-reflection-positivity-from-reeb","label":"conj:os-reflection-positivity-from-reeb","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/os-reflection-positivity-from-reeb.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}